course: dictionary
lesson: 5376
title: Knee: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. Knee is a body part, but it can also mean your lap, the part of your trousers over your knee, or a verb: to hit someone with your knee. The sentence tells you which meaning you need. In «Sit on my knee», you sit on a lap, not on a joint.
explain: Look at the words around knee. «Bend your knees» and «knee pads» are about the body joint. «Knee-deep» tells you how far up something reaches. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: Phrases can carry a meaning of their own. «Weak at the knees» is a saying about feeling very shaky with excitement or fear. «The bee's knees» was 1920s American slang for something excellent, and it was playful nonsense, so the meaning is not about bees at all.
fact: The knee is a hinge joint in the middle of your leg, where it bends.
fact: The kneecap protects the front of the knee and helps the thigh muscles pull.
fact: As a verb, «knee» means to hit someone with your knee.
fact: «Knee-deep» means reaching up to your knee, and «knee-high» means as high as your knee.
fact: In babies the kneecap is soft cartilage that turns to bone over the first years.
exercise: «Sit on my knee.» In this sentence, what does knee mean? | The joint where your leg bends | *Your lap when you sit | The part of your trousers over the knee | To hit someone
exercise: «Everyone gets older: grey hair, glasses and stiffer knees come.» What do stiffer knees mean? | Knees that are softer and more bendy | Knees that have been hit | Trousers that are tighter | *Joints that bend less easily
exercise: Which sentence uses knee as a verb? | *«He kneed the thief in the leg.» | «Sit on my knee.» | «Knee pads keep you safe.»
test: «The water was knee-deep.» What does knee-deep mean? | Deep enough to cover your whole body | *Deep enough to reach your knee | Frozen solid | Dry and warm
test: «The kneecap protects the front of the knee.» What does the kneecap do? | Bends the knee for you | Makes the knee bigger for running | *Protects the front of the knee | Stops your leg from growing
exam: Sam says the word knee always means the same thing. Is Sam right? | Yes, it always means a body part | No, it always means to kneel | Yes, it always means the part of your trousers | *No, knee can be a body part, a lap or a verb
